                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "It's been a while, but I thought it's time to revisit my favorite Steam grindhouse action game.\r\n\r\nBlast through hordes of enemies with Shank's Shotgun or Twin Pistols! Unless they're holding an AK-47 which makes them immune to bullets. Huh. That's weird.\r\n\r\nLunge through the air and pounce on unsuspecting- wait, no that doesn't work anymore. I mean, sometimes he lunges on his own, usually off a cliff. Oh well.\r\n\r\nGrab enemies and throw them into the air to execute brutal combos! Go on. Grab em. Grab the dude, Shank! Dang, I guess that doesn't work anymore either.\r\n\r\nWell, at least I can Shred enemies with Shank's signature shanks and chainsaw! Oh, actually I guess now it's more like irritatingly scratch at your enemies. Wow, that guy can really take a lot of stabbing for a little dude. Like a lot.\r\n\r\nDodge out of the way of- oh come on, seriously? Ok so you CAN still dodge, it just . . . doesn't work as a dodge anymore? I guess it helps you jump slightly farther, but they can totally hit you while you're dodging.\r\n\r\nI know some people will tell me that it's 2026 and this game is over 10 years old, and what do I expect? To which I show my middle finger while I play GOG games that are older than I am without issue.\r\n\r\nRIP Shank 2. You were a really cool game. Like a long time ago.",
